    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-11-02, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (116 hits across 27 queries, scan regenerated 2026-11-02 06:04 KST via 'bash run.sh scan', 0 source errors, collected_at 2026-11-01T21:05 UTC). Unlike the previous cycle, the score-9 top band was largely RECYCLED (GSE328275 TNBC-CD45 immune atlas, GSE328422 sequential lymph-node metastasis spatial, GSE326553 Oprm1-A118G opioid CosMx, and the GSE281463/64/65 3D-chromatin-GWAS bundle), so the actionable harvest comes from the score-6 ladder after accession-level dedupe against BOTH the page-level GSE retention set (30 accessions retained on the page) AND the full git history of the digest page, which is the stricter test used today (18 candidate accessions checked against every prior daily-digest commit; 15 had already appeared in earlier digests and were dropped). The three picks below are the accessions that have NEVER appeared in the digest page in any commit - they are therefore accession-level NOVEL against the entire published archive, not merely against the current 5-entry window. Signal 1 is GSE327909 (Homo sapiens, 3 patients, paired normal mucosa and colorectal polyp tissue including hyperplastic polyps and tubular adenomas, 31,147 high-quality cells post-QC, pdat 2026/10/31): a paired-design single-cell atlas that resolves four conserved microenvironmental hallmarks of early colorectal polypogenesis - disrupted epithelial homeostasis (stem-cell expansion, Paneth-cell reduction, Wnt activation), pro-inflammatory CD4+ T-cell polarization with Th17 expansion and NF-kB/IL-17 activation, functional reprogramming of CD8+ subsets with loss of intraepithelial lymphocytes, and extensive remodeling of immune-epithelial intercellular communication along CD55-ADGRE5, MIF-CD74 and GZMA-PARD3 axes. Signal 2 is GSE349296 (Homo sapiens, n=6, pdat 2026/10/31): a three-node intervention chain in endometrial cancer in which KLF16 - a transcription factor driving proliferative signalling across endometrial endothelial, epithelial and smooth-muscle compartments - is elevated in human tumour tissue and tracks with advanced stage and high histological grade; KLF16 knockdown inhibits proliferation in vitro and impedes tumour growth in vivo; unbiased screening nominates the lncRNA CTD-2377D24.6 as the downstream mediator; and co-immunoprecipitation plus single-cell transcriptomics show SIN3A physically interacts with KLF16, with CTD-2377D24.6 overexpression counteracting the anti-proliferative effect of KLF16 depletion. Signal 3 is GSE313015 (Homo sapiens, n=10, pdat 2026/10/21, PMID 41773915, ACS Chemical Biology, doi:10.1021/acschembio.5c01011): Li-BrU-seq, an optimized 5-bromouridine-based nascent-RNA sequencing method using one-step immunopurification that achieves genome-wide profiling of newly synthesized RNA from as little as ~500 ng total RNA (approximately 25,000 cells), with benchmark data demonstrating enrichment specificity and data quality. What links the three is a single methodological thesis for the day: THE PRODUCTIVE UNIT IS THE EARLIEST RESOLVABLE STATE - all three signals deliberately move upstream of the endpoint (pre-malignant rather than malignant mucosa; the regulatory node rather than the effector output; the nascent-transcriptome kinetics rather than the steady-state transcriptome), and each one supplies an intervention matched to that upstream position.",
